inform6: inform6 (interactive fiction compiler)
inform6:
inform6: Inform 6 is version 6 of Inform, an interactive fiction programming
inform6: language created by Graham Nelson. Inform 6 made its debut on
inform6: April 30th, 1996, and it continues to be one of the most popular
inform6: IF development systems even after the introduction of Inform 7 in
inform6: 2006. Inform 6, like all other versions of Inform, compiles to code
inform6: not only for the Z-machine, the same virtual machine used by Infocom,
inform6: but also for the more powerful and flexible virtual machine called
inform6: Glulx.
